.policy "ruff-dtz006-call-datetime-fromtimestamp" revision 2
.description "Pass a timezone when building a datetime from a timestamp; without one you get a naive local time that can't be safely compared with aware datetimes."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff DTZ006 (flake8-datetimez): `datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(ts)` without a timezone, or with `tz=None`;
// the result is naive local time. The timezone is the second positional argument or `tz=`. A call followed by
// `.astimezone()` (through any `.replace(…)`) is aware and not reported. Reported at the call. Only in a file
// that imports datetime.
//   datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(1234)                  ← DTZ006
//   datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(1234, tz=None)         ← DTZ006: None
//   datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp(1234, datetime.timezone.utc)   not reported
#include "python/datetime.rr"

.violation DTZ006(at: node) code "DTZ006"
    "Pass a timezone, e.g. `tz=datetime.timezone.utc`, so the result is aware; leave it naive only if local wall-clock time is really intended."
    suppress ruff "DTZ006"
.violation DTZ006_none(at: node) code "DTZ006"
    "Pass a real timezone instead of `None`, e.g. `tz=datetime.timezone.utc`, so the result is aware; keep `None` only if a naive local time is intended."
    suppress ruff "DTZ006"
DTZ006(c) :- naive_tz(c, "datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp", "missing"), !then_astimezone(c).
DTZ006_none(c) :- naive_tz(c, "datetime.datetime.fromtimestamp", "none"), !then_astimezone(c).
